hello everyone i'm kristen tomlin the  founder and ceo of dough cookie dough  confections and trust me i know  a thing or two about baking the perfect  cookies and welcome to pro tips from pro  chefs  i'm gonna show you all of my tips and  tricks on making sure that your cookies  turn out beautiful  and perfect and delicious every single  time first thing you're gonna need is  just a baking sheet  i like one that happens to have a rim on  it so that it's easy to grab  from the oven and any time i'm baking i  always line the sheet with parchment  paper you can find it pre-cut  in these sheets which is the way to go  because it already will fit your pan  perfectly  and you won't have to worry about  getting any cuts on that blade you also  are going to need  a cookie scoop and this is just to make  sure that all of your cookies are the  same size when baking  that way they'll spread evenly they'll  bake evenly and they'll all  look amazing so go ahead fill your  cookie scoop all the way to the top  and just when you put it on the sheet  leave a little bit of room  i usually say three fingers between each  cookie to make sure that there's enough  room for it to spread nicely  i always like to add whatever inclusions  are inside my cookies  on top to make it extra beautiful and  make sure that all those yummy mix-ins  don't fall down to the bottom  and now we're ready for the oven but  you're gonna have to make sure your oven  is fully preheated  before we stick our cookies in so mine's  already  very hot and ready to go so let's go  ahead and put it in  so halfway through baking you're going  to want to check on your cookies make  sure that everything is baking evenly  usually i like to rotate the pan and if  i have two trays  i just swap the top one with the bottom  one i can tell my cookies are just about  done because my kitchen smells delicious  and last time i peeked they're golden  brown on the outside  you're going to want to grab them and  just let them cool on the baking sheet  resist the urge to dig  in just yet let them cool here for about  five minutes but luckily because we have  this parchment paper on here  cleanup is gonna be a breeze and your  bottoms will never  ever get brown for more recipes and tips  go to thedrewberrymoreshow.com  and grab a copy of my cookbook hello  cookie dough  for lots of other recipes and tips just  like this  [Music]  huh
 

